\section{Experiment 2: PMOS Transfer \& Output Characteristics}

\textbf{Aim:}  
To plot and analyze the transfer (Id–V\textsubscript{SG}) and output (Id–V\textsubscript{SD}) characteristics of a PMOS transistor using Cadence Virtuoso (90nm GPDK).

\textbf{Objective:}
\begin{itemize}
    \item To design PMOS testbench for DC analysis.
    \item To obtain Id–V\textsubscript{SG} and Id–V\textsubscript{SD} curves.
    \item To extract $|V_{th}|$, transconductance $g_m$, output resistance $r_o$, and channel-length modulation $\lambda$.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Equipment/Software:}
Cadence Virtuoso, ADE L/XL, gpdk090 library.

\textbf{Theory:}  
A PMOS transistor conducts when the gate is sufficiently negative with respect to the source.  
Saturation region equation:
\[
|I_D| = \frac{1}{2}\mu_p C_{ox}\frac{W}{L}(V_{SG}-|V_{th}|)^2(1+\lambda V_{SD})
\]

\textbf{Procedure:}
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Create a PMOS device with source and bulk tied to VDD.
    \item Sweep gate voltage to vary V\textsubscript{SG} for transfer characteristics.
    \item Sweep drain voltage to vary V\textsubscript{SD} for output characteristics.
    \item Run DC analysis and record Id.
\end{enumerate}

\textbf{Result:}  

