\section{Experiment 3: Transient Analysis of CMOS Inverter}

\textbf{Aim:}  
To perform transient analysis of CMOS inverter using a load capacitor and analyze output behavior for different W/L ratios.

\textbf{Objective:}
\begin{itemize}
    \item To study inverter input-output waveform.
    \item To calculate rise/fall delay.
    \item To observe effect of transistor sizing and load capacitance.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Equipment/Software:}  
Cadence Virtuoso, ADE Transient Analysis.

\textbf{Theory:}  
Propagation delay:
\[
t_{pd} = R_{eq}C_L
\]
Increasing W/L reduces delay; increasing load capacitance increases delay.

\textbf{Procedure:}
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Build CMOS inverter using PMOS (W/L larger) and NMOS (W/L smaller).
    \item Apply pulse input (0–VDD).
    \item Connect load capacitor (CL).
    \item Change W/L ratios and observe delay variation.
\end{enumerate}

\textbf{Result:}  
\begin{figure}[H]
    \centering
    \includegraphics[width=0.8\textwidth]{Cmos Inverter.jpg}
    \caption{CMOS Inverter Circuit}
    \label{fig:circuit}
\end{figure}


\begin{figure}[H]
    \centering
    \includegraphics[width=0.8\textwidth]{Cmos trans .jpg}
    \caption{CMOS Inverter Output Transient}
    \label{fig:circuit}
\end{figure}








\textbf{Conclusion:}  
Inverter delay decreases with larger W/L and increases with larger load capacitor.

